# Long-form documentation.
#
# Kept out of the repository on purpose. `docs/` holds detail that goes stale faster than the
# code it describes — build walkthroughs, endpoint listings, generated design specs — and a
# published document that disagrees with the source is worse than no document. What a reader
# genuinely needs to trust lives at the root (README, ARCHITECTURE, ROADMAP, SECURITY) or in
# the code's own doc comments, which cannot drift from what they document.
#
# `docs/superpowers/` is the one exception, and for the opposite reason: a design spec records
# *why* a decision was made and which alternatives were rejected, which the code cannot say and
# which stops being recoverable once everyone who was there has forgotten. It is dated and
# historical by construction, so it does not drift — a spec from August describes what was
# decided in August whether or not the code still agrees. `docs/*` rather than `docs/` because
# git will not descend into an excluded directory, so the negation below needs a traversable path.
docs/*
!docs/superpowers/

# Release staging, written by the release workflow's artifact collector.
/dist-release/
